TY  - JOUR
TI  - Long-term abstinence after a nicotine patch: 24-month follow-up of a placebo-controlled trial in primary care
AU  - Hartmann, L.
AU  - Weiss, P.
AB  - METHODS: We followed the 412 adults aged 18 years or older who smoked and had been randomised to a 16-hour nicotine patch or a placebo patch in primary care (NCT01234561). RESULTS: Validated abstinence at 24 months was 12.1% with the nicotine patch and 6.8% with placebo. CONCLUSIONS: The benefit of the nicotine patch persisted for two years.
