TY  - JOUR
TI  - Nicotine inhaler versus placebo inhaler for smoking cessation: a randomised trial in general practice
AU  - Lindqvist, Anna
AB  - METHODS: In this randomised, double-blind trial, 247 adult smokers in general practice used a nicotine inhaler or a placebo inhaler for 6 months. RESULTS: Sustained abstinence at 12 months was 13.0% with the nicotine inhaler and 7.4% with placebo. CONCLUSIONS: The nicotine inhaler helped smokers in general practice to stop.
PY  - 2015
DO  - 10.1000/nrt.2015.077
JO  - Scandinavian Primary Care Trials
