TY  - JOUR
TI  - Nicotine mouth spray for smoking cessation: a 12-week randomised placebo-controlled trial
AU  - Moreau, Claire
AB  - METHODS: We randomised 320 adult smokers to nicotine mouth spray or placebo spray for 12 weeks. RESULTS: Abstinence at the end of treatment (week 12) was 21.3% with nicotine mouth spray and 11.2% with placebo. No follow-up after treatment was planned. CONCLUSIONS: Nicotine mouth spray increased short-term abstinence.
